				1489,
				228
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add Tier 3 service implementations\n\nAdd the remaining VS Code service implementations to Wind's Effect-TS service layer, completing the service coverage:\n\n**New Services:**\n- StorageService: Persistent key-value store backed by Mountain's StorageProvider\n- NotificationService: Toast messages and progress indicators via UserInterfaceProvider\n- ProgressService: Progress reporting with location options (notification/statusBar/window)\n- QuickInputService: Quick pick and input box dialogs via blocking IPC pattern\n- WorkspacesService: Multi-folder workspace management\n- ThemesService: Color theme get/set/list operations\n- SearchService: Text and file search via native glob/grep\n\n**Changes:**\n- Integrate all new services into TauriBaseLayer and TauriLiveLayer compositions\n- Add IPC channel handlers for each new service (notification:*, progress:*, quickInput:*, search:*, storage:*, themes:*, workspaces:*)\n- Include Problem types for each service with proper discriminated union error handling\n- Add Stub and Mock implementations for testing\n\nAlso includes code formatting standardization across all Effect files (import ordering, line wrapping, consistent style) applied during the service implementation work.",
			"SHA": "3fb587fe90c9ab08220b31472024c31d4512f088"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-05T13:40:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1405,
				14
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add Terminal and Output service implementations\n\nAdd complete TerminalService and OutputService implementations to Wind's Effect-TS service layer, completing the Terminal service from the previous commit and introducing the Output service:\n\n- **TerminalService**: Add Live implementation backed by Mountain's TerminalProvider via Tauri IPC (terminal:create, terminal:sendText, terminal:dispose, terminal:show, terminal:hide). Also add Stub and Mock implementations for testing.\n\n- **OutputService**: New service for output channel management. CreateChannel creates named channels, Append/AppendLine emit text, Clear resets panel, Show displays panel, Dispose cleans up. Backed by IPC (output:create, output:append, output:appendLine, output:clear, output:show).\n\n- **TextFileService**: Update Live implementation to use actual Tauri IPC instead of stub, adding Read, Write, Save, SaveAll, IsDirty, and Revert operations.\n\nBoth services are now integrated into TauriBaseLayer and TauriLiveLayer composition under \"Tier 2 service layers\".",
			"SHA": "2681049fa1aae54ed8c63b61b9a41fc7b77bff62"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-05T13:37:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1386,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add Terminal service interface\n\nIntroduce TerminalService interface for Wind's Effect-TS based service layer, mirroring the VS Code terminal service. The interface provides methods for terminal lifecycle management:\n\n- CreateTerminal: Creates new terminal instances with configurable name, shell path, arguments, and working directory\n- SendText: Sends input text to a specific terminal\n- Dispose: Cleans up terminal resources by ID\n- Show/Hide: Controls terminal panel visibility\n\nAlso add TerminalProblem discriminated union for typed error handling with three variants: TerminalNotAvailable, TerminalOperationFailed, and TerminalNotFound.\n\nThis follows the same pattern established for Commands, Editor, Extensions, Files, Language, and TextFile services added in recent commits.",
			"SHA": "ca8cd6f4e0c32b115ffdc496c378acef3c2f9009"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-05T13:28:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1381,
				7
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Implement Live service layers for Commands, Editor, Extensions, Files, and Language\n\nAdd concrete Live implementations for the VS Code service interfaces introduced in the previous commit. Each service now has a functional implementation backed by Tauri IPC to communicate with Mountain (Rust backend):\n\n- **CommandsService**: Local handler registry for UI-side commands with IPC delegation to Mountain's CommandRegistry for extension commands\n- **EditorService**: Editor state via Ref subscriptions with Monaco command delegation for selections/decorations\n- **ExtensionsService**: Extension discovery and activation via Mountain's ExtensionManagementService IPC\n- **FilesService**: Full filesystem operations (read, write, stat, mkdir, delete, rename, copy, exists, watch) with URI → path normalization\n- **LanguageService**: In-memory provider registration tracking with local disposal support\n\nAll implementations use Effect-TS patterns with proper error modeling via discriminated union Problem types. The services are now integrated into TauriBaseLayer and TauriLiveLayer composition.",
			"SHA": "be5579b56a30e11bde1a45b8481b38ac9a366d4e"
		},
